@startuml public_chat_event_boundary
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@7e54b47f modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeEventController.java submitEvent/listEvents
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@7e54b47f modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventProjector.java projection methods
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@7e54b47f modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/provider/openai/OpenAIResponsesProvider.java handleOutputItemAdded/handleOutputItemDone/convertToolResultInput
' Observed behavior: the current Claw HTTP layer has request-scoped POST SSE and history GET, but no independent long-lived stream GET.
' Observed identity: OpenAI Responses call_id maps to Claw ToolCall.id and is written back for Tool results.
' Pending implementation design: Mate separates event submission, live Chat observation, and authoritative fixed-snapshot history.
' Design reason: a transport disconnect must not determine whether a write succeeded or whether an execution continues.
' Architecture changes: Mate keeps eventId independent, publishes OpenAI Tool Call IDs, and returns the complete accepted user event.
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
title Public Chat - Responsibility Boundary (pending implementation)
top to bottom direction
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 35
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
actor "Authorized client" as Client
package "mate-service" {
  component "Chat Events API\nAuthentication and Chat authorization" as API
  component "Runtime bridge\nPrivate Chat to Session mapping" as Bridge
  component "Public event projection" as Projection
  database "Public complete history" as History
}
package "CampusClaw" {
  component "Session runtime" as Runtime
  database "Runtime entries" as Entries
}
Client --> API : submit / observe / reconcile
API --> Bridge : authorized command
Bridge --> Runtime : internal POST SSE
Runtime --> Entries : ordered commit
Runtime --> Bridge : normalized events
Bridge --> Projection : safety mapping
Projection --> History : full events
API --> History : fixed snapshot
Projection --> API : live preview and notification
note bottom of Projection
Public eventId and OpenAI toolCallId have separate meanings.
Bridge mappings remain pending implementation and require contract alignment.
end note
@enduml

@startuml public_chat_event_recovery
' Public evidence: Claude Managed Agents events-and-streaming docs, checked 2026-09-02.
' Source evidence: pi@5cd93f68 packages/protocol/src/schemas.ts TranscriptProgressSchema/SessionSnapshotSchema
' Source evidence: pi@5cd93f68 packages/server/src/sessions.ts handleRuntimeEvent/broadcastSnapshot
' Design reason: deltas are disposable preview while completed history is authoritative.
' Architecture change: public eventId replaces exposure of internal sequence for reconciliation.
' Presentation: one responsibility-level scenario; implementation details remain in the linked document.
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 180
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #425B70
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #BAC4CC
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #8496A4
skinparam sequenceGroupBackgroundColor #FAFBFC
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #BAC4CC
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFBEF
skinparam noteBorderColor #D2C6A5
hide footbox
autonumber

title Recover One Public Chat View - Pending implementation
participant Client
participant "Mate Chat API" as Mate
participant "Runtime bridge" as Bridge
database "Public history" as History
Client -> Mate : Open public stream; submit message once
Mate -> Bridge : Submit using private Session mapping
Bridge --> Mate : Accepted user event
Mate --> Client : Complete JSON receipt
Bridge -->> Mate : Normalized output
Mate -->> Client : Preview and same-ID complete events
... Observation disconnects ...
Client -> Mate : Reopen stream and request history
Mate -> History : Read complete pages from fixed snapshot
History --> Mate : Authoritative events
Mate --> Client : Complete history pages
Client -> Client : Deduplicate; replace matching preview
note over Client,Mate
  Public stream stays open across idle and later executions.
  User events appear in receipts and history, not the live stream.
  Numeric paging integration remains pending.
end note
@enduml
